The two .jsonl.gz files in this directory are derived data, not source code.
They are licensed separately from the rest of nass, and separately from each
other: they come from different upstream projects with different licences, so
they are shipped as two files and merged in memory at load time.

nouns.jsonl.gz
    Source
        English Wiktionary, https://en.wiktionary.org
        Extracted with Wiktextract, https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Arabic/
        Upstream file: kaikki.org-dictionary-Arabic.jsonl, built 2026-10-30
        sha256 19eee17681c23b3da039878ee7c970d93b75a339989a17a842f14aa7f44ea236

    License
        Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported (CC BY-SA 3.0)
        https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

    Modifications
        Only the plural and dual cells of the declension tables for nouns,
        adjectives and proper names were kept. Entries whose every sense is an
        inflected form (tagged form-of) were dropped. Each row was reduced to
        the lemma, its plural and dual forms, a sense count and a short gloss.
        The result is 10,860 rows covering 9,223 lemmas.

arramooz.jsonl.gz
    Source
        arramooz, https://github.com/linuxscout/arramooz
        Arabic Dictionary for Morphological analysis, noun tables in
        data/nouns/*.csv, cloned 2026-11-14

    License
        GNU General Public License, version 2
        https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html

    Modifications
        The singular and plural columns of the noun tables were read in both
        directions. A cell such as "+ات" was expanded to the sound feminine
        plural; cells mixing several notations were dropped. Rows were kept
        only for lemmas that the Wiktionary extract does not already give a
        plural for, and only when the lemma is not itself a plural. The result
        is 9,898 rows.

Rebuild with tools/build_data.py and tools/extract_arramooz.py. Those scripts
are MIT like the rest of nass; these data files are not.
